Louanna’s actress soul was admirable, but to an even greater extent than he trying to lay down
on the ground, he wanted to avoid letting her act out what had happened this time. Only, he had
no intention whatsoever of making it so that had never happened.
Heinkel was descended from a House of Knights, a man of the Kingdom who ought to be honest
and sincere.
Ergo――,
Heinkel: [Louanna, I don’t intend on letting what I said there conclude as a means to an end. I
don’t ever want to do anything that would embarrass you like that.]
Louanna: [Heinkel-san…]
Heinkel: [The organization might have been crushed, but there’s a worry that remnants might
still target you. In order to extinguish that, it would be best for you to stay with us. So…]
Louanna: [――――]
Heinkel: [So, won’t you marry me for real?]
Louanna: [Let me see~, I refuse~.]
An instant rejection.
At the cheerfulness and lightheartedness of that response, for a moment, Heinkel almost pat his
chest in relief. As if the marriage proposal he had summoned all his courage into had gone well.
But, that was not the case.
Louanna had said it clearly. She refused.
Heinkel: [W-wh-wh-why?]
Louanna: [Didn’t I tell you? I still have to pay off my House’s debts. With those circumstances
remaining, I can’t allow myself to get married, much less to Heinkel-san of House Astrea.]
Heinkel: [Those debts, I’ll pay them on your behalf…]
Louanna: [But would that really be your own money, Heinkel-san? Not your family’s money.]
Heinkel: [No, that’s…]
Louanna: [If that’s the case, then it’s a no~. Or rather, even supposing it was actually
Heinkel-san’s money, I could never allow you to pay it on my behalf~. This is my own problem,
after all.]
Placing a hand over her chest, Louanna firmly declared so, leaving Heinkel at a loss for words. It
was excessively upright and sound reasoning from a moral standpoint.
But, when it came to an undaunted sound argument, Heinkel also had one.
Heinkel: [But, the matter of the remnants could still very well be dangerous. In order to protect
against that as well…]
Louanna: […As well?]
Heinkel: […Won’t you at least make the part about being my fiancée true?]
If he might say so himself, when he put it to words, he was astounded from the bottom of his
heart at how ungallant of a confession it must have been.
If only he could have done it more smoothly, a flawless marriage proposal that would be blessed
by everyone universally, akin to that of his parents that continued to be sung about in the Sword
Demon Love Song; that would have been Heinkel’s ideal. Even now, Heinkel found himself
unable to follow in the example of his parents.
Louanna: [Might I ask, why?]
Heinkel: [Eh?]
Louanna: [Why, are you willing to go so far for me, Heinkel-san? Even if you say it’s because
you’re a Knight, we’re talking about the person you’re going to be spending the rest of your life
with.]
Heinkel: [That’s…]
At Louanna’s earnest question, Heinkel gulped down his breath, and fell into deep
contemplation.
What came to mind were reasons like, because he would not go back on his word, or because it
was a man’s duty to take responsibility. But, probably, it was neither of those things. Those
words were borrowed, words that did not belong to Heinkel.
The reason why Heinkel Astrea had asked Louanna Hartley to marry him, that was――,
Heinkel: [――Because, you’re special. We still barely know each other, but I want to know you
more, I want to speak with you more. I wanna be by your side. That’s my reason.]
Falteringly, yet with words that were not borrowed, Heinkel conveyed how he truly felt.
Receiving that, Louanna placed a hand to her own cheek, and gazed at Heinkel.
Her blue eyes were moist, her white cheeks were blushing, and with a slight quiver in her voice,
she spun her next words.
Louanna: […Spoyous.]
Heinkel: [Sp-spoyous?]
Louanna: [Super duper, joyous~.]
Hearing her response, Heinkel blinked his eyes, and this time, he did pat his chest in relief.
If it was in front of her, Heinkel Astrea could hold his head high as a Knight. ――Without any
evidence save for the warm feelings budding in his heart, Heinkel thought so.
――Heinkel Astrea, and Louanna Hartley who was now his fiancée. The passionate love between
the two who would go on to be wed, would lead to a future that shook the Dragon Kingdom of
Lugunica, one that shook the very world.
However, in this very moment, unaware as to what their future held in store, the young man
who had displayed his bravery, and the young woman who harbored a faint affection for him,
simply shared a heartwarming moment, and that was all.
《Fin》
